 {"$schema":"fabro-journal-v1","run_id":"01M20T9S8JRXETASN64768TRRP","node":"reviewer","visit":1,"status":"succeeded","ts":"2026-09-08T16:25:33Z","data":{"painpoints":[{"text":"Seed fabro-06e0 (run 01M20T9S8JRXETASN64768TRRP): two acceptance-critical files (.fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro inspects declaration, prompts/planner.md step 4 rewrite) were classified as loop-churn in the evidence capture, showing counts only (+8/-1, +1/-1) with no diff — yet they are seed spec requirements. I had to reconstruct them with `git diff 9eeab20 -- <paths>`. Fix idea: the evidence classifier should treat files named in the in-progress seed spec as seed-work (full diff) even when they live under .fabro/, so reviewers without shell access are not forced into Changes-requested on unread evidence."}],"observations":["Verified with tools beyond the capture: workflow.fabro declares inspects=\"develop\" and fabro_tools=\"fabro_runs_list\"; planner.md step 4 now uses fabro_runs_list with only state==\"open\" counting as in-flight, journals 'skipped: in-flight PR <n>', continues down sd ready, and explicitly prohibits gh/direct GitHub API. fabro_tools is graph-level so all stages receive the read-only runs_list tool — no write capability added, judged acceptable.","ADR-0019 check: the GET /runs/{id}/pull_request route widening (RequireRunScoped → RequireRunManagementTarget) is an agent-reachable authz change but is exactly the seed's recorded user decision D1, read-only, least-privilege direction; mutating PR routes keep the strict extractor. No new credentials, tools, or gh.","Live verification (a develop pass journaling 'skipped: in-flight PR <n>' against an open gate PR) is deferred by construction — it can only be produced by the next develop run; all offline acceptance criteria and unit/integration tests pass. Watch for that journal line on the next develop pass as the closing proof.","The id=\"local\" test pinning in server/tests.rs is a documented 6-line adjacent repair for a pre-existing Docker-socket break reproduced on parent commit 22e03c3 — legitimate, minimal, and covered by a full crate suite run."]}}
